  "result": "Perfect! All 352 tests pass. Here's a summary of the bulk discount implementation:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation Summary\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Added `bulkDiscount(line)` function** in `src/totals.js`:\n   - Returns 0 if qty < 10\n   - Calculates 2.5% of (lineTotal - lineDiscount) for qty >= 10\n   - Applied after the line's own/tier discount\n\n2. **Updated `lineVAT(line)`** in `src/totals.js`:\n   - VAT base now calculated as: lineTotal - lineDiscount - bulkDiscount\n   - VAT is on what remains after both discounts\n\n3. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** in `src/totals.js`:\n   - Discount field now sums lineDiscount + bulkDiscount for all lines\n   - Total calculation properly reflects all discounts\n\n4. **Exported `bulkDiscount`** from `src/invoices.js` for backwards compatibility\n\n**Tests Added** (18 new tests in `test/totals.test.js`):\n- bulkDiscount returns 0 for qty < 10\n- bulkDiscount calculates 2.5% for qty >= 10\n- Bulk discount applied after line discount\n- lineVAT with bulk discount calculations\n- invoiceTotals includes bulk discount in total discount\n- Mixed quantities (some with bulk, some without)\n- Interaction with vouchers and multiple VAT rates\n\n**Updated existing tests** that had quantities >= 10 to use quantities < 10 or updated expected values to account for bulk discount.",
